Non-tunneled traffic, involving interference between satellite beams and terrestrial systems, requires addressing external interference. Techniques like satellite diversity and relay diversity are employed to mitigate interference. Satellite diversity allows multiple satellites to share beams, and relay diversity uses other satellites as relays to help manage interference. These strategies enhance resource sharing and reduce interference impact.

