The extraction of features from encrypted flows in the proposed ML framework necessitates additional power and bandwidth margins, particularly at the link level. This is because decryption of encrypted data, such as AES or RSA keys, consumes power and bandwidth. Without decryption, features extracted from encrypted flows cannot be reliably identified, leading to security vulnerabilities. Additionally, the link-level encryption, which may require multiple links in satellite communications, further increases resource consumption. Therefore, the framework must ensure secure decryption processes and optimize network architecture to minimize power and bandwidth usage, thereby maintaining link margins and secure communication.

